    "score": 4,
    "assessment": "Repository fit is generally good. The implementation is localized, reviewable, and avoids new top-level roots or family drift. The only deduction is that promoting content whose tests/docs contradict the code would inject confusion into the canonical tree."
  },
  "shared_common_assessment": {
    "score": 5,
